<pdd-reason>Route prompt processing exclusively to an explicitly configured llama.cpp/OpenAI-compatible server without paid-provider keys, GitHub authentication or cloud fallback.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
{"name":"get_local_llm_config","signature":"(cwd: Path | None = None) -> LocalLLMConfig | None","returns":"Validated immutable endpoint configuration or None"},
{"name":"local_llm_environment","signature":"(config: LocalLLMConfig) -> dict[str, str]","returns":"Non-secret settings pinned for nested PDD commands"},
{"name":"invoke_local_llm","signature":"(config: LocalLLMConfig, messages: list, *, temperature: float, output_pydantic=None, output_schema=None, use_batch_mode=False, max_output_tokens=None, max_input_tokens=None) -> dict","returns":"PDD result, model, zero API cost, separate thinking, usage and endpoint provenance"},
{"name":"local_llm_estimate","signature":"(config: LocalLLMConfig, messages: list, *, command: str, max_output_tokens=None) -> dict","returns":"Provider-free approximate estimate with zero API charges"}
]}}</pdd-interface>

Implement pdd/local_llm.py. Frozen LocalLLMConfig includes base_url, model
(default auto), max_tokens (8192), timeout (600 seconds), optional temperature,
optional context_window, optional enable_thinking and api_key_env (default
PDD_LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY). Configuration stores only an environment-variable
name, never a literal key. No API key or placeholder is required.

Discover nearest project boundary (.pddrc or .git) walking from cwd. Read
.pdd/local_llm.json ahead of the top-level .pddrc local_llm mapping, and use
~/.pdd/local_llm.json only if the project specifies neither. An explicit
PDD_LOCAL_LLM_CONFIG file overrides discovery. PDD_LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL,
PDD_LOCAL_LLM_MODEL, PDD_LOCAL_LLM_MAX_TOKENS and PDD_LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT override
file fields. Serialized PDD_LOCAL_LLM_CONFIG_JSON pins inherited non-secret
settings ahead of file discovery; local_llm_environment returns that mapping
along with PDD_LOCAL_LLM_ENABLED=1 and PDD_FORCE_LOCAL=1 for child commands.
PDD_LOCAL_LLM_ENABLED=0 explicitly disables this mode (useful for
mocked-provider tests); a configured empty/malformed endpoint fails closed.
Accept HTTP(S) local/LAN addresses including IPv6 and DNS. Append /v1 to a bare
origin; preserve supplied API prefixes. Reject userinfo, queries, fragments and
wildcard bind addresses with an actionable connect-address message.

Use shared OpenAI-compatible /models and /chat/completions HTTP interfaces,
independent of native Metal vs Linux CUDA/container launch details. If model is
auto, require exactly one advertised model and use its exact id. Do not query
model catalogs or fetch weights. Reject redirects. Disable ambient proxies and
netrc credentials. Read only the configured dedicated key variable, if present.

Output uses llm_invoke's result contract: Pydantic requests return a validated
model instance, raw JSON-schema requests return a validated JSON value, normal
requests return final text. Separate reasoning_content from content. Batch
items execute sequentially on the same server and aggregate local token usage.
HTTP/model/schema/empty/truncated-output errors fail with endpoint guidance,
never copied response bodies or secrets. A thinking-only response is incomplete.
Require finish_reason=stop for a completed non-streaming answer. JSON-schema
validation MUST NOT retrieve external reference resources over the network.
Do not execute returned tool calls in this transport.

Estimates make no network calls, including discovery/tokenization. Label the
UTF-8 serialized-message byte count as a conservative input approximation, not
a measured tokenizer count. Admission respects configured/command output caps,
and optional input/context limits using that same conservative bound. API cost
is zero (hardware/electricity costs are not estimated). Sampling can be explicitly
configured per local model; otherwise use the caller's temperature. Optional
enable_thinking maps to chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking.

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Resolve configuration from the nearest project, machine-local override or explicit environment without modifying caller settings.
R2 (MUST NOT): Contact a cloud provider, GitHub, model catalog or credential prompt in local endpoint mode or after an endpoint failure.
R3 (MUST): Send requests only to the configured validated endpoint with the exact configured/discovered model and bounded output/timeout.
R4 (MUST NOT): Forward ambient paid-provider credentials, proxy settings, netrc auth or follow HTTP redirects.
R5 (MUST): Support plain text, validated Pydantic/JSON schema output and sequential batches while separating reasoning from final answers.
R6 (MUST NOT): Return empty, malformed, tool-only or token-truncated responses as final output.
R7 (MUST): Keep estimates network-free and mark approximate token counts and zero API charges explicitly.
R8 (MUST): Behave identically for macOS/native and Linux/container HTTP servers, including loopback and explicit LAN addresses.
</contract_rules>

